KARAOKE-CLOCK-001 controller gate log (2026-11-08 night)

ROOT CAUSE (device-proven on the OLD binary):
- Clean-data-dir install carried media/words.jsonl (4,819 rows); sidecar
  row for the shown clip verified with exact entry id and span 0.0-1.44 s.
- Audio provably played (PipeWire sink-inputs 0 -> 1 during Play).
- Pixel sampling: zero accent-soft (#E2EEEB) chip pixels in idle AND
  mid-playback frames (identical #F5F1E9 regions) -> the karaoke chip
  never lit. Clock link dead: timeupdate delivered no events on the
  short blob clip.

FIX (this commit):
- attachKaraokeClock in word-timing.ts: rAF pump over currentTime,
  timeupdate kept as second source, startAt seek + stopAt pause kept.
- Playing state on the shadowing Play button (label + aria-busy).

GATES:
- npx tsc --noEmit -> clean.
- npx vitest run src/word-timing.test.tsx -> 11/11 (3 new pump tests,
  incl. the zero-timeupdate regression pin).
- npx vitest run (full) -> 47 files / 354 tests.
- pnpm fmt:check -> all prettier-clean.
- Rust untouched by this lane; cargo gates run before commit.

DEVICE RE-VERIFY STATUS (honest):
- Rebuilt release binary contains the fix (Playing label + pump in the
  built asset; AppDir/binary rebuilt 22:22 after the change).
- Xvfb re-test environment proved unreliable: the AppImage web process
  crashed at startup (appsink/autoaudiosink not found -> GLib-CRITICAL;
  a frozen last-painted frame made all clicks look dead), and the raw
  binary run degraded differently (focus landed on an editable field on
  the card; stray keys produced junk text - separate UX smell, filed in
  notes). Audio never reached PipeWire in the degraded instances.
- Verdict: unit-level regression pinned; in-webview chip pixel-sample
